Creating the shared object(.so) library:
----------------------------------------
Fxx directory contains F77, F90 and few C files, for the most part matches with
the ACES II distribution. The key-diffrence is that they are no longe executable.
They all are now libraries. For book keeping purpoes the ACESII structue remains
intact, and we need to buils shared libriaries conrrespondig to subroutins in
each subdiectory. We use the same ACESII makefile structue (GNUmakefile, GNUmakefile.src
and the top level ACESII_SOURCE_DIR/makefile). 

Use clean.py if you need to delete all the old links to GNUmakefle and GNUmakefile.src
(only needed in a new machine or if old links are broken)

For Intel commpilers the compiler flags to buld a shared library:

ifort -traceback -shared -fPIC -O2 -Zp8 -zero -i8 -o XXX.so and build the archive 
files. 

Steps:
module load intel/verison python/3.11
From toplevel (home/Fxx directoy)
python clean.py (if needed)
gmake clean
gmake 
Each subdirectory contains shared library archive with *,a wrong extension.
Then use makelibso.py (python makelibso.py) to rename all the XXX.a files to XXX.so

Left to do: Eliminate intermediate XXX.a files. 


